From 44d2e171c2270e2d20aa576f9648b0706d32c478 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Dagunts <ddagunts@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:02:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Match LG's DDK 1.9@2291151 interface: drop TI-only
 additions

The TV's userspace (libsrv_um.so etc., DDK 1.9@2291151 cobra_lg_linux) is
built against IMG's 1.9 interface; TI's tag adds to it:
- PVRSRV_MISC_INFO: cache op regions (sRegions etc.) and the CUSTOM_FLUSH,
  CUSTOM_INV, CLEAN_REGIONS, INV_REGIONS cache ops (grows the struct and
  GET_MISC_INFO/GETCLIENTINFO by 88 bytes)
- bridge commands REMAP_TO_DEV, UNMAP_FROM_DEV, IMPORT_GEM after
  EXPORT_DEVICEMEM_2, which shift every later bridge number by 4
- pfnSwapToDCSystem in the display class jump table

Checked against LG's pvrsrvkm.ko: all 195 interface types in the headers
lay out the same (DWARF), and the bridge dispatch table is identical
(104 entries).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
